add({
0:('Can one model segment brain tissue, regions and lesions across lifespan MRI?','BrainSeg unified uni/multimodal learning with synthetic augmentation.','Evaluates45,998 scans from26 datasets with strong internal and external Dice performance across three segmentation tasks.','Segmentation accuracy is an imaging endpoint, not proof of improved clinical outcomes.'),
1:('Can EHR screening identify atypical undiagnosed PNH?','Structured/unstructured EHR algorithm with Monte Carlo feature selection.','Screening1.3million patients led to119 flow-cytometry referrals and13 diagnoses, highlighting atypical presentations.','Referral completion and selected testing affect yield; modeled avoidable delays are retrospective.'),
2:('Does self-supervised sleep EEG capture health information beyond stage labels?','Transformers pretrained on unlabeled overnight recordings with matched controls.','Representations recover sleep stages and finer microstructure; clearest advantages over stage supervision concern BMI and age.','Effects on other outcomes are smaller or unreliable; pretraining gains are task-specific.'),
3:('Can baseline retinal images predict anti-VEGF response in vein occlusion?','GAN image synthesis, UNet++ lesion analysis and ResNet-101 prediction.','Evaluates576 patients and clinician assistance; external retreatment prediction is weaker than internal performance.','Reader improvements and plausible generated images do not establish treatment-outcome benefit.'),
4:('Can LLMs calculate thrombosis-risk scores from narrative records?','Delphi-derived expert prompting for Padua/Caprini across six open models.','Tests held-out hospitals and finds high item agreement, with weaker Caprini risk-category agreement.','Retrospective score extraction does not establish reduced thromboembolism under AI-guided prevention.'),
5:('Can retinal foundation representations predict incident atrial fibrillation?','RetiAF retinal embeddings with optional clinical-feature fusion.','Evaluates UK Biobank and Shanghai data, outperforming conventional scores in internal comparisons.','External discrimination declines and exploratory ischemic-heart associations do not prove causal cardio-retinal mechanisms.'),
6:('Can calibrated cumulative risk improve football injury decisions?','Survival-informed ML with beta calibration and decision-theoretic thresholds.','Four seasons of elite women’s football data support improved discrimination and fatigue-related predictors.','Single-team observational evidence does not establish transferable injury-prevention effects.'),
7:('Are sequential Gemini-generated radiology study materials safe without review?','Seven-stage multi-LLM text/image pipeline evaluated by residents and attendings.','Blocking errors exceed the predefined safety threshold; feedback changes evaluator scrutiny rather than demonstrating automation safety.','Single-arm rereview and a small image pilot cannot isolate feedback effects or justify autonomous deployment.'),
8:('Can surgical video phases support automated skill assessment?','AI-miSMG deep workflow recognition across five procedural phases.','Multicenter testing reaches0.87 accuracy and reduces annotation time while enabling fluency comparisons.','Workflow recognition and experience associations do not establish validated surgical competence or patient benefit.'),
9:('How do relational vulnerabilities modify conversational-AI mental-health outcomes?','Three-arm randomized conversational intervention with engagement/mediation analyses.','Among977 students, AI improves anxiety and well-being; loneliness and insecure attachment predict engagement and improvement.','Student selection and mediation assumptions limit causal interpretation of relational mechanisms.'),
10:('Can automated pediatric arousal detection reduce scoring variability?','PANDA contextual U-Net encoder–decoder over multichannel polysomnography.','Large development/test cohorts and adjudicated platinum labels show stronger agreement than CAISR; external calibration helps.','Performance depends strongly on reference-label quality and cohort-specific adjustment.'),
11:('Can routine oral photographs classify and delineate leukoplakia?','Conditional deep classification followed by interpretable lesion segmentation.','Tests778 training images and193 external cases, retaining approximately90% diagnostic accuracy.','Image classification does not predict future malignant transformation or replace biopsy confirmation.'),
12:('How do LLM psychiatric item ratings compare with clinicians?','Ten-model AMDP scoring of simulated interview transcripts.','Best models approximate upper-middle clinician performance but show different missing-information/error patterns.','Only three simulations are used; transcript-only models and audiovisual clinicians receive different information.'),
13:('Can brain-metastasis MRI predict EGFR subtypes?','Adaptive LightGBM radiomics with SHAP/LIME and matched transcriptomics.','Analyzes1,303 lesions from421 patients and validates prediction against pathology, with sphericity-related biological correlations.','Lesions are nested within patients; molecular associations and model explanations do not establish mechanism.'),
14:('How much does home ECG acquisition degrade hospital-trained models?','Lead-I deep models with cross-device validation and labeled fine-tuning.','Hospital transfer is relatively stable, while Apple/QOCA recordings show substantial loss recoverable with sufficient adaptation data.','Small fine-tuning sets can harm performance; outputs remain screening or triage estimates.'),
15:('Can general LLMs encode EHRs without private clinical pretraining?','Natural-language code descriptions converted to downstream embedding features.','Matches CLMBR across15 EHRSHOT tasks and improves selected UK Biobank outcomes.','Portability gains trade off against computational cost and do not eliminate vocabulary/domain shift.'),
16:('Can retinal foundation models support dementia risk stratification?','Comparison of five vision encoders and fine-tuning strategies.','RETFound-MAE performs best in a36,000-plus Korean population and predicts later incidence.','Medication-linked disease definitions and ethnic concentration require broader validation.'),
17:('Can conversational agents prepare patients before catheterization?','Sofiya customized LLM voice workflow with nurse escalation.','Prospective implementation across1,431 patients maintains high call completion after stabilization and reduces system errors.','Single-center operational success does not establish clinical safety or nurse-time savings causally.'),
18:('Can degraded slit-lamp images still support keratitis diagnosis?','Simulated degradation, improved GAN restoration and lesion-aware classification.','Multicenter image evaluation shows high diagnostic discrimination despite low-quality inputs.','Restoration may alter diagnostic detail; image-level validation is separate from real-world clinical effectiveness.'),
19:('How reliable is histology AI for neoadjuvant-response prediction?','PRISMA systematic review with QUADAS-2 quality assessment.','Twenty-five studies show promising discrimination but only about40% report external validation.','Heterogeneous acquisition, validation units and incomplete sharing restrict cross-study comparison and translation.')})
add({
20:('Can report filtering establish pathology-reduced CT reference distributions?','Five-LLM evidence-grounded ensemble followed by covariate-adjusted distributional modeling.','Filters350,000-plus examinations to construct volume/attenuation charts for106 structures and examines longitudinal changes.','Report-negative cohorts are pathology-reduced, not proven healthy; acquisition and contrast remain important covariates.'),
21:('Which macrophage methylation programs accompany colorectal chemotherapy resistance?','Multi-omics ML prognostic signatures with mechanistic validation.','A six-gene signature and SCG2-related macrophage–tumor signaling link risk with5-FU resistance phenotypes.','Large pooled sample counts and prognostic associations do not establish clinical reversal of resistance.'),
22:('Can under-pillow ballistocardiography support accurate sleep monitoring?','BCGNet PSG pretraining followed by modality-transfer fine-tuning.','Nearly596,000 recorded hours support staging, apnea estimation and sleep-architecture validation across cohorts.','Hours are repeated recordings rather than independent participants; contactless agreement is not treatment efficacy.'),
23:('Can structured genetic knowledge improve rare-disease reasoning?','KGRD specialist agents combine knowledge graphs, genomic/phenotypic inference and verification.','Benchmarks420 cases and improves top-diagnosis quality and composite evaluation scores.','Retrospective case-benchmark gains do not establish prospective diagnostic yield or counselling safety.'),
24:('Can AI agents replace physicians as clinical-response evaluators?','Matched human/agent assessment of free-text answers to real de-identified cases.','More than400 physicians show experience-dependent rankings; agents align directionally but miss clinical nuance.','Evaluator heterogeneity and simulated agent personas limit substitution for expert assessment.'),
25:('Can sensor-derived gait maps reveal shared functional phenotypes?','Topological data analysis plus supervised gait-signature learning.','Maps81 people across neuromotor conditions and identifies clinically aligned stroke subgroups.','Small heterogeneous cohorts and cross-sectional clusters do not demonstrate tailored rehabilitation benefit.'),
26:('Can scoliosis planning and postoperative alignment be modeled together?','YOLO-derived segmentation plus latent-diffusion radiograph prediction.','Evaluates1,425 patients using retrospective development and prospectively collected validation cohorts.','Prospective collection alone does not establish that an unchanged model improved surgical outcomes.'),
27:('Do endpoint scores conceal unsafe oncology-note reasoning?','Hierarchical error taxonomy applied to successive GPT models and automated evaluators.','Structured biases are associated with harmful recommendations; newer models reduce but retain these patterns.','Retrospective note interpretation and preliminary mitigation do not establish safe deployment.'),
28:('Can multilingual grounded chatbots support polio surveillance communication?','AFP Assistant fine-tuning with retrieval augmentation in three languages.','Expert-curated questions and human evaluations support response grounding, relevance and usability.','In-house response testing does not establish improved case detection or community reporting rates.'),
29:('Can AI help surgeons recognize pelvic anatomy?','Image-trained anatomical segmentation evaluated during short-video recognition.','Thirty-six surgeons improve sensitivity/specificity with assistance on640 snippets.','Short-snippet observer performance does not establish continuous intraoperative utility or reduced complications.'),
30:('Can federated learning unify lifespan brain-connectome analysis?','FedFound self-supervised pretraining and distributed disease-specific refinement.','Evaluates22,911 subjects and nine diagnostic tasks, identifying shared and disorder-specific morphology.','Cross-task accuracy does not establish prospective clinical benefit or remove site heterogeneity.'),
31:('Can frozen pathology be translated into more interpretable permanent-section images?','Comparison of four unpaired generative translation architectures.','CUT provides strongest image fidelity; generated images improve reassessment concordance in selected discrepant cases.','Image realism and selected-case concordance do not guarantee preservation of every diagnostic feature.'),
32:('Can ultrasound-specific instruction data improve vision–language reasoning?','SonoInstruct curation and Qwen3-VL fine-tuning evaluated with SonoBench.','Multi-source data improve eight capabilities, including out-of-distribution tests, relative to the base model.','Instruction instances are not patients; benchmark gains require clinical-setting validation.'),
33:('How is remote psychiatric consultation associated with subsequent service use?','Adjusted diagnosis-stratified logistic regression of longitudinal EHR cohorts.','Most groups show no worse associations, but schizophrenia-spectrum patients have higher hospitalization/emergency odds with remote use.','Observational associations cannot establish noninferiority or causality; the abstract does not describe a substantive learned-AI intervention.'),
34:('Can keyboard language identify adolescent suicidality reliably?','Youth-specific NLP lexicon validated against LLMs and human-coded messages.','Millions of entries across two high-risk cohorts show associations with suicidal histories and current ideation.','Jokes, hyperbole and third-person content complicate intent; text entries are nested within adolescents.'),
35:('What evidence supports trustworthy cuffless blood-pressure AI?','Systematic taxonomy of sensing, modeling and calibration with reporting guidance.','Identifies protocol realism, calibration drift, population diversity and fairness gaps.','A methodological framework does not demonstrate clinical validity of every reviewed monitor.'),
36:('Can MRI localize recurrent glioma rather than only classify patients?','Interpretable ML of pathology-coordinate MRI patches with uncertainty analysis.','Patch testing maps recurrence heterogeneity; map volumes associate with survival in56 additional patients.','Patches and tissue samples are not independent patients, and survival association is not causal.'),
37:('Can steroid-based screening reduce medication washout for aldosteronism?','Feedforward neural and other ML models using steroids/potassium with optional renin.','Renin-independent models outperform aldosterone/renin ratio and reduce false positives across1,380 patients.','Threshold-specific screening accuracy does not establish cost-effectiveness or patient-outcome improvement.'),
38:('Can routine multiplanar MRI reconstruct fibroids without new annotations?','FGAS foundation-guided domain adaptation with anatomical pseudo-labels and view consistency.','Improves reconstruction Dice over baseline across clinical cross-domain datasets.','Pseudo-labels and sparse image coverage can propagate errors; segmentation improvement is not surgical benefit.'),
39:('Can surgical gestures be linked automatically to recovery?','F2O spatial/temporal transformers and frame-level gesture classification.','Learned gesture features approximate human annotations and associate with erectile-function recovery after prostatectomy.','Outcome associations do not show that changing gestures causally improves recovery.')})
add({
40:('Can confocal corneal images support automated reports and patient questions?','IVCM-Insight contrastive image–text learning with domain-adapted LLM dialogue.','Image/report testing and specialist ratings support structured interpretation and relevant explanations.','Text-overlap metrics and expert ratings do not establish prospective diagnostic safety across systemic/corneal conditions.'),
41:('Can angiography retain temporal detail at lower acquisition rates?','Angio-FILM latent flow matching interpolates missing video frames.','Expert assessments favor generated videos, while anatomical lumen measurements show small deviations.','Quantitative image metrics are mixed; visual realism does not prove reduced-radiation procedures preserve every clinical finding.'),
42:('Can EHR phenotypes reveal comorbidity-linked premature-aging groups?','Unsupervised clustering with onset-age, genetic and mortality analyses.','Identifies70 clusters among100,272 eMERGE patients and replicates high-risk profiles independently.','Age, sex and survival selection shape clusters; associations do not identify causal aging mechanisms.'),
43:('Can multimodal models warn of ocular GVHD after transplantation?','GVHD-MLLM latent fusion across four modalities and multiple tasks.','Internal and external evaluations support diagnosis/severity prediction and assisted junior-reader performance.','Early-warning discrimination drops externally; observed treatment-seeking severity differences are not randomized intervention effects.'),
44:('Can one vision–language model interpret laboratory morphology?','Lingjian multistage Qwen3-VL adaptation with grounding supervision.','Performs strongly on national quality-assessment cases and improves junior-reader sensitivity in120-case testing.','EQA and observer studies are distinct from prospective routine-laboratory diagnostic outcomes.'),
45:('Can multimodal lung-cancer prognosis tolerate absent imaging streams?','Foundation-encoder features with missing-aware intermediate fusion.','Integrates available CT, pathology and clinical variables without complete-case exclusion, outperforming unimodal/fusion baselines.','Survival stratification in the available cohort does not establish intervention benefit or broad external transportability.'),
46:('Can voice agents streamline super-resolution ultrasound workflows?','DeepSeek-R1 command parsing with MiniCPM-V image interpretation.','Automates acquisition parameters, reconstruction and structured reports assessed by14 clinicians.','Report structure and workflow feasibility are not validated patient diagnosis or improved clinical outcomes.'),
47:('Can renal-replacement decisions be personalized dynamically?','HRRT hierarchical reinforcement learning spanning initiation, modality, ultrafiltration and weaning.','Retrospective multinational evaluation estimates lower mortality under learned recommendations.','Off-policy mortality estimates are counterfactual, not observed survival gains in a randomized treatment trial.'),
48:('Which human–AI collaborations show empirical healthcare benefits?','JBI/PRISMA scoping review of140 studies.','Evidence concentrates on diagnostic interpretation and short-term tasks, with inconsistent outcome definitions.','Few longitudinal patient/system outcomes or empirical governance evaluations support broad effectiveness claims.'),
49:('Can fetal-ultrasound representations generalize across tasks?','FetalCLIP paired image–text foundation pretraining.','Tests classification, gestational age, congenital-heart detection and segmentation with limited labels.','210,035 images are training units, not independent pregnancies or demonstrated screening-outcome benefit.'),
50:('Can childhood congenital kidney disease progression be predicted at several horizons?','POCC general and hereditary-feature ML risk models.','Develops models in2,249 children and tests pediatric/general-hospital external cohorts and online deployment.','Population differences affect external accuracy; prediction does not establish improved renal outcomes.'),
51:('Can pathology estimate heterogeneous PARP-inhibitor benefit?','Treatment-aware deep survival modeling of PAOLA-1 randomized data.','An ETI score stratifies progression benefit among421 patients with pretreatment slides beyond HRD status.','This is secondary trial-data modeling, not a new model-guided randomized trial; external validation remains necessary.'),
52:('How are clinical tasks divided between clinicians and AI?','Scoping synthesis of85 healthcare collaboration papers.','Links collaboration patterns to task risk/automation and identifies broader efficiency/user-experience evaluation.','Conceptual task patterns do not demonstrate comparative safety or patient benefit across applications.'),
53:('Can brain-tumor segmentations express useful calibrated uncertainty?','Evidential deep ensembles model meningioma boundaries and volume credibility.','Internal, independent and external testing show high Dice and uncertainty aligned with ambiguous regions.','Good calibration in evaluated cohorts does not guarantee detection of every distribution shift.'),
54:('Can lesion-focused learning reduce gender bias in skin diagnosis?','LesionAttn attention constraints with Pareto performance/fairness selection.','Two dermatology datasets show reduced gender disparities while retaining malignancy discrimination.','Dataset fairness gains need evaluation across other demographics and real clinical settings.'),
55:('What do young people need from mental-health chatbots?','Mia codesign workshops with reflexive thematic analysis.','Thirty-two participants emphasize transparency, personalization and integration without replacing human care.','Qualitative design preferences are not evidence of chatbot therapeutic effectiveness.'),
56:('Does a full day of ECG improve future heart-failure prediction?','DeepHHF long-record deep learning with explainability.','Holter analysis outperforms short segments and a clinical score, linking high-risk predictions with hospitalization/death.','Retrospective prediction and saliency do not prove preventable outcomes or causal cardiac mechanisms.'),
57:('Can physician expertise and EMRs improve clinical language models?','AI4Doctor curriculum fine-tuning and reinforcement alignment across instructional sources.','Expert/benchmark evaluation supports richer clinical responses from combined knowledge sources.','Subjective response quality and benchmark comparisons do not establish safe autonomous consultation.'),
58:('Can distributed longitudinal modeling match pooled-data analysis?','PEAL one-shot federated spline mixed-effects estimation.','Simulations recover parameters and systemic-sclerosis data demonstrate multi-institution disease trajectories.','Lossless statistical equivalence concerns the specified model, not unrestricted privacy or arbitrary predictive models.'),
59:('Can multiple pathology stains jointly classify coronary disease?','UNICORN stain-specific experts plus transformer interaction aggregation.','MISSION lesion testing improves severity classification and reveals cross-stain tissue phenotypes.','Cross-sectional severity recognition does not itself demonstrate longitudinal disease-progression prediction.')})
add({
60:('Can first-contact narratives support acute-coronary triage before laboratory results?','TriageMaster-70B language modeling of narratives and vital signs.','Reports high sensitivity in retrospective cases and an author-described prospective pilot, with faster processing than retrospective cardiologist review.','Previously inspected Methods contain an unresolved prospective-pilot/model-release chronology conflict; prospective validation timing remains unconfirmed.'),
61:('How do ChatGPT answers compare with nuclear-medicine staff responses?','Prospectively collected patient queries scored using QUEST dimensions.','Experts generally rate generated responses favorably, especially administrative answers, while nonexpert preferences differ.','Ratings and rater agreement vary; no trial demonstrates improved patient understanding or clinical safety.'),
62:('Can AS-OCT quantify infectious keratitis more consistently?','Semi-supervised U-Net/Swin segmentation with lesion parameterization and3D visualization.','Image testing supports tissue/lesion delineation and high agreement on infiltration dimensions.','Agreement with annotated images does not establish improved treatment decisions or vision outcomes.'),
63:('How has software-containing device authorization changed?','Regulatory-document text analysis identifies digital components across device categories.','Finds substantial growth over two decades with differences across specialties.','Digital-device identification and authorization counts are not evidence of AI efficacy or postmarket safety.'),
64:('Can contactless multinight monitoring address sleep-apnea variability?','AI-enabled under-mattress measurement compared with single-night polysomnography.','Most analyzed participants achieve sustained home recordings; disagreements align with variable sleep position and duration.','Small selected cohort and imperfect reference-night capture limit claims of definitive misdiagnosis correction.'),
65:('Do digital dermatology interventions improve quality of life?','Systematic review of fourteen telemedicine and patient-support studies.','Telemedicine is often comparable or better, while communication/tracking effects vary.','Heterogeneity, bias and short follow-up limit pooled conclusions; AI is mainly a proposed future component.'),
66:('When should medical language models abstain instead of answer?','Review plus decision-theoretic MedSAFE clinical-dialog evaluation.','Distinguishes uncertainty-driven from safety-driven abstention and demonstrates a proof-of-concept framework.','Sparse realistic benchmarks and pilot evidence do not establish an optimal clinical refusal policy.'),
67:('Does bone geometry encode ACL-injury susceptibility?','ACL-P point-cloud deep classification of3D morphology.','Multicenter and athlete evaluations show robust injury-status discrimination across trauma phases.','Post-injury classification is a proxy for structural susceptibility, not direct prospective injury prediction.'),
68:('Can breast histology suggest ATM pathogenic-variant status?','Whole-slide deep classification with histological pattern analysis.','Discovery and replication samples support discrimination and immune/lobular-like morphological associations.','Small carrier datasets and lower replication balanced accuracy preclude replacing genetic testing.'),
69:('Can LLMs detect depressive-state changes from behavioral streams?','Few-shot prompting, embedding features and QLoRA on digital phenotyping.','LLM approaches outperform traditional baselines, with strategy-dependent single-feature versus multimodal strengths.','Clinical validation and safeguards remain necessary before longitudinal monitoring affects care.'),
70:('What is the translational evidence for malaria diagnostic AI?','Scoping comparison of microscopy, rapid tests and deep parasite detection.','Reviews promising automation and access benefits across endemic/nonendemic contexts.','Annotation inconsistency and underrepresented endemic populations restrict generalizable diagnostic claims.'),
71:('Can combined ultrasound/CT/MRI approximate ovarian-cancer MDT decisions?','OVUCM radiomics with intermediate fusion and nested validation.','Tests five preoperative tasks and externally compares predictions with specialists and consensus.','MDT-level diagnostic agreement does not show better treatment selection or survival.'),
72:('Can synthetic medical images improve demographic equity?','FairGen physician-preference-aligned diffusion generation.','Tests dermatology, chest radiography and MRI with subgroup improvements and independent evaluation.','Synthetic subgroup coverage and selected fairness measures do not establish equitable real-world outcomes.'),
73:('Can wrist actigraphy screen REM sleep behavior disorder across devices?','ActiTect standardized preprocessing and interpretable motion-feature ML.','Nested, blinded and independent-cohort tests support cross-dataset discrimination.','Screening accuracy does not confirm diagnosis or predict conversion to neurodegenerative disease.'),
74:('How effective are CBT-based NLP conversational interventions?','Meta-analysis of fifteen randomized trials involving1,737 participants.','Finds depressive-symptom and negative-affect benefits, while several other outcomes lose significance after bias adjustment.','Subgroup/moderator findings are preliminary and do not imply uniform efficacy across chatbot designs.'),
75:('Can autonomous agents combine clinical data with medical knowledge?','LLM-derived hybrid graphs powering ED-specific prediction and recommendation tools.','Benchmarks show task-dependent improvements in triage, interactions, readmission and medication recommendation.','Graph size and retrospective task gains do not establish safe autonomous emergency decisions.'),
76:('Can LLMs accelerate biomedical data-standard harmonization?','GPT-4 metadata generation plus weighted ElasticSearch semantic matching.','Experts validate generated common-data elements; ADNI/GP2 tests show partial mapping of unseen headers.','High metadata acceptance differs from complete interoperability; semi-structured data remain harder.'),
77:('Can ICU interventions be predicted jointly rather than independently?','FIRST-ICU graph/LSTM encoders with intervention-interaction attention.','MIMIC-IV and untouched AmsterdamUMCdb tests support forecasting and interpretable patient grouping.','Predicting existing treatment patterns is not evidence that recommended treatments improve outcomes.'),
78:('How can explainable models inform young-athlete cardiac risk?','Systematic synthesis of incidence, arrhythmia xAI and electrophysiological modeling.','Reviews84 studies and identifies fragmented definitions and dominant saliency techniques.','Separate epidemiological/modeling evidence does not constitute a validated combined athlete-risk system.'),
79:('Can live EHR sequences warn of next-day hypoglycemia?','Bayesian-tuned LSTM using medication, nutrition and laboratory histories.','Outperforms baseline models and remains stable in prospective daily evaluation.','Precision is modest and live prediction does not show that acting on alerts prevents hypoglycemia.')})
add({
80:('Can ocular-ultrasound foundation models stratify vision and tumor risk?','SonoEye contrastive image–text pretraining and Eye-RADS tiered classification.','Large paired training supports18-disease differentiation, reporting and external risk agreement.','External agreement is lower than internal results; age effects differ and clinical outcomes remain untested.'),
81:('Can habitual movement jointly indicate frailty and fear of falling?','Entropy activity barcodes and attention-based bidirectional-LSTM multitask learning.','Forty-eight-hour recordings from146 people support both questionnaire-linked classifications.','Small cohort and surrogate labels do not establish prospective prediction of falls or functional decline.'),
82:('Can trial-grounded LLMs answer informed-consent questions reliably?','Documentation-constrained answering with human and moderator-model scoring.','Responses score highly for technical accuracy, but humans disagree about contextual adequacy and empathy.','This is foundational answer testing, not participant-facing proof of informed understanding or consent quality.'),
83:('Can shared clinical-code embeddings support grounded patient modeling?','ClinVec embeds a large clinical-vocabulary knowledge graph.','Clinician validation supports semantic relatedness and applications in QA, stratification and risk prediction.','Semantic similarity and downstream demonstrations do not guarantee factual reasoning across all codes.'),
84:('Does AI improve recognition of ampullary lesions?','Standalone endoscopic classification plus assisted observer comparison.','Fellows and general endoscopists improve, while subspecialists show no significant overall gain.','Retrospective images require prospective video validation before intra-procedural benefit can be claimed.'),
85:('Can routine antenatal measurements stratify PPROM risk?','Longitudinal multimodal XGBoost with SHAP explanations.','Laboratory/ultrasound data identify CRP and albumin as important late-gestation features.','Measurement count is not pregnancy count; predictive attribution does not establish inflammatory causation.'),
86:('Can contrastive models standardize clinical-skills assessment?','Learned performance representations with automated proficiency scoring.','Procedure-specific validation shows high score agreement and immediate-feedback potential.','Peak accuracy under selected settings does not demonstrate competence transfer or improved patient safety.'),
87:('Can foundation-model adaptation be federated efficiently?','Fed-GPL patient-customized generative prompts across vision encoders.','Tests retinal/melanoma classification and polyp/prostate segmentation with limited parameters and communication.','Federated optimization does not by itself guarantee privacy or performance at unseen institutions.'),
88:('Which spectral architectures generalize across clinical and vector-surveillance tasks?','MALDI-TOF deep-learning/preprocessing benchmark with compute/energy analysis.','Tests mycobacterial identity/resistance and mosquito species/age across7,424 spectra.','Spectra are nested within isolates/specimens, and deployment trade-offs differ across tasks.'),
89:('Does AI-assisted swallowing rehabilitation produce sustained benefit?','Systematic review with GRADE certainty and NASSS implementation assessment.','Short-term supervised gains coexist with declining adherence and attenuated effects after cessation.','Evidence for unsupervised care, other etiologies and durable outcomes remains insufficient.'),
90:('Can lightweight networks segment spinal anatomy in real time?','EndoSeg-RT reparameterized convolutions with multiscale attention/fusion.','Tests labeled endoscopy images from61 patients and transfers to dental segmentation.','Image benchmarks do not establish continuous-operation safety or reduced surgical injury.'),
91:('Can generative models forecast MRI while preserving patient identity?','IP-DDGAN metadata conditioning and identity-preserving regularization.','Synthetic longitudinal images retain morphometric and disease-related features and support progression modeling.','Plausible generated trajectories are not observed patient futures or validated intervention-response predictions.'),
92:('Can AI-guided novice ultrasound complement ECG screening?','Two-step AI-ECG and guided focused-ultrasound acquisition with expert interpretation.','Prospective referral-cohort testing reduces imaging use while maintaining strong predictive values.','Two-step screening loses sensitivity versus imaging everyone; lower-prevalence populations need validation.'),
93:('Can lumbar MRI quantify biological aging patterns?','Contrastive slice-ensemble age prediction with imaging-derived age deltas.','Multicenter testing supports age estimation and preliminary longitudinal biomarker behavior.','Initial longitudinal examples are proof of concept, not validated degenerative-risk intervention targets.'),
94:('Can raw MALDI spectra support identity and antimicrobial decisions?','ANTIBIOTIC LightGBM identity models, temporal-convolution resistance models and LLM interface.','Species identification transfers well, but resistance accuracy collapses temporally and improves only partly after updating.','High internal AMR performance cannot be generalized without drift monitoring; chatbot recommendations lack outcome validation.'),
95:('Can agents turn noisy clinical recordings into useful training corpora?','Planner–Memory–Executor transcription correction and dialogue structuring.','Controlled comparisons and ablations support reconstruction gains; cleaned-data fine-tuning improves expert/HealthBench scores.','Limited English portability and curated evaluation do not establish robust multilingual real-world communication.'),
96:('Can federated models tolerate incomplete CT contrast phases?','FedOG orthogonal gradient decomposition with Bayesian update selection.','Five-institution and public-data tests show modest segmentation improvements under phase heterogeneity.','Dice gains do not establish prospective lesion-detection benefit or privacy guarantees.'),
97:('Can clinicians steer interpretable prediction-model discovery?','HACHI iterative AI concept search with yes/no linear models.','AKI and brain-injury tasks show useful concepts and cross-site/time generalization.','Human review remains essential for concept granularity, bias and leakage detection.'),
98:('Can proteomic clocks capture eye-specific aging and disease?','ML protein-age models integrated with deep imaging phenotypes.','Cross-national discovery/validation links accelerated aging with major ocular diseases and neural–vascular changes.','Aging associations and predictive biomarkers do not establish causal pathways or treatment effects.'),
99:('Can a fundus photograph encode angiographic dynamics?','Fundus2Video autoregressive GAN with transferable retinal representations.','Expert assessments and ten external task datasets support generative fidelity and representation transfer.','Generated angiography cannot establish patient-specific unobserved perfusion or replace invasive testing without further validation.')})
add({
100:('What limits individual cognitive-trajectory prediction in Parkinson disease?','Ten ML families with synthetic signal/noise controls across PPMI/NACC.','Coarse screening trajectories remain poorly predicted, while richer neuropsychological measurements improve discrimination.','Low measurement fidelity limits the attainable signal; added model complexity or genetics does not resolve it.'),
101:('Can guideline-only knowledge graphs improve ophthalmic dialogue?','EyeRAG GraphRAG across six LLMs and several retrieval configurations.','Expert/scenario testing shows better grounded communication and fewer hallucinations than vanilla models.','A120-scenario benchmark supports supervised counselling assistance, not autonomous diagnostic decisions.'),
102:('How accurate is imaging AI for lung-cancer metastases?','Task-specific systematic review and meta-analysis.','Pooled discrimination is promising across molecular, differentiation and outcome tasks.','Substantial between-study heterogeneity and best-model selection restrict direct clinical extrapolation.'),
103:('Can weakly supervised foundation transfer localize prostate cancer?','ProViCNet patch-level contrastive MRI learning with optional PSA fusion.','Multicohort tests and reader comparison support lesion detection and improved specificity in a virtual screening scenario.','Potential biopsy reduction is inferred, not observed in a randomized screening pathway.'),
104:('Which factors predict quality-of-life change after Parkinson DBS?','Explainable random forest using symptom subscores and electrode coordinates.','Finds age, emotional burden and right-subthalamic placement associated with improvement in130 patients.','Modest held-out discrimination and observational explanations do not establish optimal causal placement rules.'),
105:('Can ChatGPT assist complex neuropathy diagnosis?','Real-case comparison with specialist/non-specialist neurologists and assisted revisions.','Matches non-specialists but trails specialists on leading diagnosis; assistance improves selected assessments.','Standardized case summaries and revision experiments do not establish real-consultation patient benefit.'),
106:('Can routine blood tests estimate colorectal-cancer survival?','Comparison of seven survival models with SHAP interpretation.','Random survival forest performs best and transfers with varying accuracy across two external centers.','Prognostic associations and variable site performance do not establish model-guided treatment benefit.'),
107:('Can staged medical training improve radiology vision–language models?','RadiSim-CL curriculum from foundational concepts through anatomy to reasoning.','Twelve-million-pair pretraining supports24 zero-shot subtasks and stronger complex-diagnostic performance.','Image–text pairs are not patients; benchmark reasoning gains require clinical workflow validation.'),
108:('Can paraspinal-muscle MRI features improve fracture-risk modeling?','Automated foundation segmentation plus federated/radiomic and clinical fusion.','Five-institution testing supports accurate segmentation and better discrimination than clinical-only inputs.','Image-derived risk signatures do not show that acting on predictions prevents fractures.'),
109:('Can offline mobile AI improve generalist skin-lesion triage?','Fine-tuned MobileNet-V3 integrated with five priority levels.','Two clinical evaluation phases show improved assisted triage and fewer unnecessary referrals.','Phase-specific comparisons and reported workflow effects do not establish long-term cancer outcomes.'),
110:('Can OCT organoid segmentation be both fast and scale-consistent?','DICE-2DSeg physical enhancement with graph interslice aggregation.','Testing93 volumes preserves much of3D-model accuracy with markedly faster processing, including tiny drug-responsive remnants.','Organoid quantification is a screening-enabling method, not proof of patient-specific treatment effectiveness.'),
111:('Can pretreatment data identify immunotherapy hyperprogression risk?','HOPE CT/clinical transformer fusion with interpretability analyses.','Retrospective multicenter testing outperforms unimodal baselines but drops from0.801 internally to0.687 externally.','Moderate external discrimination and treatment-selected cohorts limit deployment and causal response claims.'),
112:('Can functional and clinical drug similarities improve synergy prediction?','DSimSynergy graph convolution/attention combines networks, molecular features and expression.','Independent benchmarks support improved combination prediction and candidate pathway explanations.','Predicted synergy and pathway attribution need direct mechanistic and prospective therapeutic validation.'),
113:('How do general multimodal LLMs perform on nail disease?','Prospective comparative image assessment against17 dermatologists.','Free models substantially underperform clinicians, especially for tumors.','Exploratory image cases and variable models preclude standalone use; larger representative testing is required.'),
114:('Can Mamba pathology models predict breast chemotherapy response?','MCEN needle-biopsy modeling with optional clinicopathological fusion.','Five-hospital evaluation supports response discrimination, with clinical information improving performance.','Response prediction does not establish benefit from changing therapy according to the score.'),
115:('Which depression iCBT personalization strategies have supporting evidence?','Narrative evidence framework across preparation, stratification and dynamic adaptation.','Engagement optimization and initial-support stratification have stronger evidence than adaptive treatment changes.','Engagement and clinical response are distinct, and depression-specific adaptive trials remain limited.'),
116:('What predicts medical students’ dependence on generative AI?','Sequential survey regression and educator thematic interviews.','Links self-reported reliance with expectancy, pressure and social influence, inversely with critical thinking.','Cross-sectional self-report associations do not establish that AI use causes dependence or impaired skills.'),
117:('What clinical outcomes do deployed LLM studies actually measure?','Systematic evidence mapping of studies and registered trials.','Finds heterogeneous outcomes, inconsistent efficiency effects and lower/variable accuracy in randomized designs.','Reporting deficiencies and design heterogeneity prevent a general effectiveness conclusion.'),
118:('Can home-sensor behavior flag cerebrovascular risk?','Contactless multimodal prediction over fourteen-day behavioral windows.','Tests diagnosis and prodromal risk tasks in1,224 older adults with promising discrimination.','Only28 prodromal individuals underlie repeated windows; independent clinical validation remains necessary.'),
119:('Can musculoskeletal radiograph pretraining generalize across diseases?','SKELEX self-supervised vision foundation modeling and reconstruction-based localization.','Twelve tasks support label efficiency, with external bone-tumor validation and an application prototype.','External evidence is strongest for bone tumors, not uniformly proven across all musculoskeletal uses.')})
add({
120:('Can ED records identify children likely to return with asthma?','Calibrated boosted trees versus small open LLMs with environmental/social features.','LGBM performs best in post-pandemic validation and highlights prior utilization and complexity.','Temporal validation supports risk estimation, not proof that AI referrals prevent exacerbations.'),
121:('Do magnetic cardiac signals yield useful physiological representations?','MCG2Vec contrastive learning of raw64-channel recordings.','Task probes discriminate coronary disease, low ejection fraction and AF risk with distinct attribution patterns.','Attribution plausibility and single-population discrimination require broader clinical validation.'),
122:('How does AI interact with health-related stigma?','Scoping review categorizing measurement, uptake, amplification and reduction.','Seventy studies mostly measure stigma, concentrating on mental health and few reduction interventions.','Inconsistent definitions and limited cross-cultural/real-world evaluation constrain generalizable conclusions.'),
123:('Can generative tests audit the semantic consistency of EHR data?','Medical Data Pecking uses literature-grounded RAG to generate executable checks.','Three dataset demonstrations identify mismatches with epidemiological expectations.','Discrepancies may reflect genuine errors or legitimate cohort selection; neither is automatic proof of invalid data.'),
124:('Can mixed neuroendocrine lung-tumor morphology stratify prognosis?','GTBIS interpretable pathology deep learning with multi-omics correlation.','Multicenter modeling separates SCLC-like and LCNEC-like patterns associated with different survival.','Prognostic subgroup differences do not establish that phenotype-guided treatment improves outcomes.'),
125:('Can automated metrics reliably rank hospitalization-question answers?','Clinician-reference-anchored evaluation of28 AI systems.','Across100 cases, automated rankings closely align with human ratings of relevance, evidence use and medical knowledge.','Reference-dependent ranking agreement does not independently establish answer correctness or patient comprehension.'),
126:('Do AI and rule-based conversational interventions reduce distress?','Random-effects meta-analysis with robust handling of within-study dependence.','Forty-eight randomized trials show small-to-moderate reductions in depression, anxiety and stress.','Mixed agent types and variable populations prevent attributing pooled effects specifically to modern generative AI.'),
127:('Can routine pediatric data identify respiratory pathogens earlier?','Pathog-PDx interpretable clinical/laboratory multiclass modeling.','Large multicenter development and independent prospective testing support22-pathogen discrimination.','Diagnostic prediction does not replace microbiological confirmation or prove improved antibiotic outcomes.'),
128:('Can shortcut risks be detected across medical data modalities?','G-AUDIT quantifies attribute utility/detectability relative to task labels.','Image, text and tabular demonstrations uncover potential dataset shortcuts missed by qualitative checks.','Detected association risks require context-specific confirmation; auditing does not guarantee bias-free deployment.'),
129:('What randomized evidence supports AI-delivered CBT?','Systematic review with Cochrane bias appraisal and thematic synthesis.','Few included trials show significant anxiety or depression improvements, with tentative population/design moderators.','Quality concerns and preliminary subgroup patterns argue against uniform efficacy claims.'),
130:('Can automated stroke lesion processing support cognitive prognosis?','Deep segmentation and location/network prediction with LLM report generation.','Models developed in604 patients are applied to153 independent patients with close manual-pipeline concordance.','Pipeline agreement and predictive accuracy do not establish that generated reports improve rehabilitation outcomes.'),
131:('Can anomaly models flag possible reflux missed by negative monitoring?','One-class SVM/SVDD using waveform/statistical pH features with SHAP.','Finds subtle anomalies within acid-exposure-negative records and suggests candidates for reassessment.','Anomalies are not confirmed GERD diagnoses; the system complements rather than replaces conventional assessment.'),
132:('Can lipid structure explain pancreatitis risk beyond triglyceride quantity?','DeepLipiDecipher knowledge-guided molecular/metabolic graph learning.','Retrospective classification identifies structural lipid patterns and nominates an immunometabolic axis.','Computational causal/pathway inference requires experimental confirmation and does not establish a therapeutic target.'),
133:('Can a compact model estimate thrombosis after endometrial-cancer surgery?','SVM feature elimination and SHAP from perioperative clinical data.','Four retained variables support internal and independent external discrimination.','Postoperative biomarker availability and observational feature associations do not establish preventive treatment benefit.'),
134:('How consistent is LLM causal reasoning about HIV treatment?','Scenario-based testing across association, intervention and counterfactual levels.','Agreement declines for harder causal queries and experts identify realism/grounding weaknesses.','Model-generated scenarios are not independent ground truth; inaccessible citations further weaken reliability.'),
135:('Can vision–language seizure recognition transfer across environments?','EpiVLM structured prompts and fixed decision thresholds.','Tests clinical/home/public recordings with low video-level false detections and short delays.','Segment-level observations are nested within patients; prospective remote-care effectiveness remains untested.'),
136:('What does virtual dental simulation achieve before AI integration?','Scoping review of knowledge/procedural simulators and evaluation methods.','Most studies report learner gains, while AI-driven patients/tutors remain an emerging direction.','Long-term retention, clinical fidelity and implementation burden limit inference about patient-care benefit.'),
137:('Can rectal-cancer models compare regimen-specific response probabilities?','MRI/clinical hard-gated mixture-of-experts prediction.','Validation and prospective tests support response discrimination and identify hypothetical escalation/deintensification candidates.','Higher model-estimated counterfactual response is not an observed treatment gain or randomized regimen-selection result.'),
138:('Can constrained LLM rewriting improve surgical-trial abstract reporting?','GPT-4o pipeline with expert-validated CONSORT completeness scoring.','Rewrites of651 trial reports improve methodological detail and modestly improve readability.','Reporting improvements in silico do not establish factual perfection; editorial oversight remains necessary.'),
139:('Can standardized ECG data improve transferable representation learning?','CODE-II cardiologist-reviewed labels with neural pretraining and external benchmarks.','Provides millions of exams, a public subset and blinded test set across66 classes.','Public subset/test exams are not additional patients to sum; dataset transfer is distinct from clinical outcome benefit.')})
add({
140:('Can synthetic EEG be added without harming new-patient generalization?','Teacher confidence gates plus fail-closed validation selection.','Chronic-pain and motor-imagery experiments reduce harmful augmentation runs compared with ungated data.','Gating reduces rather than eliminates harm; synthetic windows remain strongly distribution-shifted.'),
141:('Can biopsy triage preserve differences among nephrologist judgments?','Expert-specific ML models combined by majority vote.','Three-cohort evaluation reproduces diverse expert patterns and shows pathology abnormalities among recommended cases.','Agreement with experts is not proof of necessary biopsy or improved clinical outcomes; prospective validation is required.'),
142:('Can open wound data support multimodal diagnosis benchmarks?','SurgWound annotations and three-stage WoundQwen interpretation/reporting.','Provides686 expert-annotated images and structured visual-question/report tasks.','Dataset creation and benchmark reasoning do not establish prospective infection detection or healing benefit.'),
143:('Can a hepatic safety score personalize systemic liver-cancer therapy?','Random-forest MHSS with independent validation and treatment simulations.','Predicts portal-hypertension/decompensation risk and identifies regimen-associated benefit/bleeding differences.','Reported reductions under simulated selection are hypothetical, not observed randomized outcome improvements.'),
144:('How reliable is LLM extraction from breast pathology reports?','PRISMA systematic review with PROBAST+AI/TRIPOD+AI appraisal.','Nine studies show strong study-specific accuracy but gaps in external validation and fairness reporting.','Tasks, targets and metrics differ, so best reported accuracies are not directly comparable.'),
145:('Can angiography classify whether intermediate lesions warrant stenting?','Attention-enhanced EfficientNet trained with functional/intravascular reference labels.','Retrospective multicenter testing shows strong external discrimination, lower than internal accuracy.','Decision-label prediction does not establish safe replacement of adjunct testing or improved intervention outcomes.'),
146:('Does prostate pathology AI help in real reporting workflows?','Prospective commercial-system assistance across three NHS centers.','Selected second reads change diagnoses; concurrent assistance reduces turnaround and immunohistochemistry use.','Workflow-dependent observational effects and potential management changes are not randomized patient-outcome benefits.'),
147:('How can LMIC-led communities strengthen responsible global-health AI?','Structured case analysis of the AI4GH community-of-practice roadmap.','Describes collaboration, local capacity and ethical/regulatory knowledge-sharing outputs.','Organizational lessons do not establish comparative health-system or patient effectiveness.'),
148:('Can surgical videos receive reproducible qualitative training scores?','AI GOALS assessment compared with experts in a prospective simulator study.','Fifty residents’ porcine procedures show high repeatability and expert agreement.','Simulation score concordance is distinct from clinical surgical competence or improved patient safety.'),
149:('How do cloud and edge surgical-AI deployment compare?','End-user usability evaluation with operational cost/carbon measurements.','Cloud improves task completion but increases strain, expense and emissions in the tested setup.','Infrastructure-specific results from23 users do not establish general superiority for every operating-room configuration.'),
150:('Can tablet eye tracking retain Parkinson-related oculomotor differences?','Simultaneous iPad/reference recording and compact three-feature classification.','Group effects align across devices and selected features discriminate12 patients from19 controls.','Small convenience samples and group-level agreement do not establish population screening validity.'),
151:('Can fine-tuned reasoning models guide rare-disease genetic testing?','RareDAI guideline-question CoT and self-distillation for Llama/Qwen.','Internal/external tests improve panel-versus-exome/genome recommendations over baseline models.','Plausible reasoning and guideline agreement do not establish higher diagnostic yield or cost-effectiveness.'),
152:('Can unlabeled facial-expression data support autism classification?','CREViT combines contrastive learning, autoencoding and vision transformers.','Dataset experiments report improved fine-grained representations and classification generalization.','Facial-image discrimination is not a validated standalone autism diagnosis or evidence of clinical utility.'),
153:('Can cancer-associated thrombosis risk be updated throughout treatment?','Longitudinal EHR transformer with quarterly prediction horizons.','VA development and Harris Health validation outperform static scores with evolving patient history.','Risk discrimination does not demonstrate benefit or bleeding safety of model-guided anticoagulation.'),
154:('How might clinical AI support or undermine person-centered care?','Critical literature reflection using a person-centered practice framework.','Identifies opportunities and relational/ethical implementation tensions through structured synthesis.','Conceptual recommendations are not an empirical comparison of AI care outcomes.'),
155:('Can one MRI system detect and distinguish glioma from metastasis?','BTSC-Net multitask segmentation/classification and visual CAD support.','Seven-center testing and junior-reader experiments improve accuracy and reading efficiency.','Assisted observer performance does not establish downstream treatment or survival benefit.'),
156:('Can dynamic corneal biomechanics reveal early keratoconus?','Video Swin Transformer with temporal attribution and mechanical assays.','Finds strong suspect-case classification and rebound-related signals supported by tissue biomechanics.','Case discrimination and correlated mechanical markers require prospective validation before screening deployment.'),
157:('Can irregular EHR history support interpretable dementia risk monitoring?','GRU-DA combines missingness decay with RETAIN-style attention.','External testing supports long-horizon prediction, strongly dependent on data completeness.','Encounter availability and attribution variability limit interpretation as stable individualized causal risk.'),
158:('Can CT-free PET correction adapt to new scanners/tracers?','CrossPET-Adapt statistical modulation and few-shot factor-map fine-tuning.','Multicenter/multitracer testing favors adaptation to unseen domains over joint training alone.','Few-shot adaptation uses target-domain information; performance is not unchanged-model zero-shot generalization.'),
159:('Can weather improve dynamic cardiac-arrest risk estimates?','Nested case-control XGBoost combining clinical and daily meteorological variables.','Environmental features improve discrimination and high-specificity predictive value versus comparator models.','Low absolute positive predictive value and case-control sampling limit population alarm-use claims.')})
add({
160:('Can synthetic minority-class fundus images improve glaucoma screening under severe class imbalance?','AUBADE-syn combines optic-nerve-centered diffusion augmentation with structured classifier ensembles.','On EyePACS with a 1:30 imbalance, AUROC reached 0.992; ten independent datasets and three fine-tuning datasets supported discrimination and calibration gains.','Retrospective image benchmarks do not establish screening effectiveness in a newly recruited clinical population.'),
161:('Can pathology AI predictions be explained through recognizable tissue morphology?','MorphoXAI links expert-interpreted morphological patterns to both global model behavior and individual whole-slide predictions.','Across tissue types and prediction tasks, explanations reflected model-associated morphology; human evaluations found useful diagnostic features and interpretable slide regions.','Explanation usefulness does not independently establish improved patient diagnosis or validate causal biological mechanisms.'),
162:('Can a foundation model connect deep phenotypes to disease subtypes and future risk?','ukbFound tokenizes individual traits from 502,118 UK Biobank participants into position-free sequences.','It identified prognostically distinct subgroups in 53 of 289 diseases and improved lifestyle-based risk prediction over ten benchmarks; the highest-risk gout group had 17.5-fold greater future odds.','Biobank associations and retrospective prediction require independent population validation before clinical risk-guided interventions.'),
163:('Can institutions collaborate on pathology AI with much lower communication costs?','FedDFP shares compact client-specific prompts applied to whole-slide patch embeddings rather than full model parameters.','TCGA-IDH and CAMELYON benchmarks showed more than 99.9% lower communication, faster convergence, and AUC gains over local and federated baselines across feature extractors.','Benchmark federation and limited parameter sharing do not alone prove deployment privacy guarantees or clinical benefit.'),
164:('Can drug-response models connect tumor transcriptomes with interpretable drug mechanisms?','BioGDR combines predicted gene-expression and kinase-inhibition features with pathway graph neural networks and drug-guided attention.','Evaluations supported compound screening and cell-line sensitivity prediction, with clinical-cohort analyses and experimental testing of an ALDH1B1 inhibitor supporting mechanistic relevance.','Preclinical sensitivity and cohort generalization do not demonstrate that model-selected treatments improve patient outcomes.'),
165:('What separates physicians’ optimism about AI from actual clinical use?','A multilingual cross-sectional survey analyzed 1,049 physicians across 50 countries and territories using regression and group comparisons.','Although 80.2% expected clinical improvement, 27.8% reported use; formal training and institutional AI availability were strongly associated with adoption.','Self-selected survey responses and cross-sectional associations cannot establish that training or investment causes adoption.'),
166:('Do datasets or algorithms explain sex-related accuracy disparities in healthcare prediction?','Ten classifiers were compared across three clinical datasets and controlled sex-ratio sampling scenarios.','Dataset identity explained 63.4% of disparity variability, versus 9.7% for algorithm choice; balancing reduced but did not remove gaps.','Three datasets and accuracy-gap metrics cannot represent every protected group, fairness definition, or deployment setting.'),
167:('Can cardiac remote-monitoring data be collected for prospective AI evaluation within routine workflows?','PASTEC uses a browser extension for pseudonymization, structured annotation, and centralized academic storage.','A prospective one-week usability comparison covered 1,276 recordings; annotation increased median review time from 2.88 to 5.31 seconds, with no identifiers detected in reviewed outputs.','This evaluates infrastructure and workload, not prospective diagnostic accuracy or clinical effectiveness of an AI model.'),
168:('Can stroke outcome prediction use rich MRI information without requiring every training feature at inference?','Autoencoder MRI embeddings, clinical variables, and imaging biomarkers were combined with privileged-information learning.','Development on 974 cases and external validation on 738 supported 90-day disability prediction; reported test AUC was 0.801 with modular performance comparable to convolutional approaches.','Predictive performance does not show improved treatment decisions; training-only information availability requires careful deployment matching.'),
169:('Does clinician engagement influence the yield of AI ECG screening for liver disease?','A post hoc analysis compared high- and low-engagement clinicians within the intervention arm of the cluster-randomized DULCE trial.','Among 110 clinicians and 1,385 alert-positive patients, high engagement was associated with substantially greater liver-disease detection and diagnostic yield.','Engagement was not randomized; this secondary comparison cannot establish a causal engagement effect or constitute a new patient-randomized trial.'),
})
add({
170:('What prevents camera-based pulse measurement from becoming clinically reliable?','A roadmap combines systematic review, technical synthesis, and a clinic-acquired remote-photoplethysmography demonstration.','It maps eight technical domains and reports strong signal agreement with reference monitors, emphasizing motion, lighting, skin-region selection, and device variability.','Proof-of-feasibility signal agreement is not evidence of diagnostic utility across diverse patients or uncontrolled settings.'),
171:('Which implementation barriers should healthcare AI deployment plans address?','A scoping review and framework synthesis consolidate implementation constructs using affinity diagramming.','FAIIR-H organizes 63 constructs into 12 domains covering development, organizational readiness, deployment, safety, and equity, providing a structured planning and evaluation tool.','A synthesized framework requires empirical testing; it does not establish that using the framework improves implementation outcomes.'),
172:('Can personal health records support individualized healthy-life-expectancy estimates?','Survival analysis is combined with multiple-imputation machine-learning ensembles and model explanations.','The model predicted one-year loss of healthy life with AUPRC nearly twice random performance and conditioned estimated survival functions on individual risk.','The abstract lacks absolute discrimination, external validation, and a sample count; learned lifestyle relationships are not causal effects.'),
173:('How familiar are medical AI developers with regulatory frameworks?','An online survey of 122 developers compares awareness, familiarity, and organizational adoption.','Only 33.6% reported formal organizational adoption, despite strong perceived developer responsibility; adopting organizations and senior developers generally showed greater familiarity.','Self-reported, cross-sectional developer perspectives do not measure product compliance or establish causal organizational effects.'),
174:('Can intraoperative physiology identify infection risk before surgery ends?','Machine-learning models summarize vital-sign trajectories into interpretable trends and distributions, with SHAP attribution.','Across 10,719 procedures, intraoperative features achieved AUROC 0.88 and outperformed preoperative-only models, with calibration across major procedure clusters.','Retrospective risk prediction does not establish that end-of-surgery alerts prevent infections or transfer reliably to other hospitals.'),
175:('Does removing screening copayments increase acceptance of autonomous retinal AI?','A randomized factorial vignette study tested copay size and sponsor among 248 adults with type 1 diabetes.','Waiving a $50 copay increased stated AI selection from 43% to 81%, but participants still preferred human reconfirmation, including after normal AI results.','Hypothetical choices measure stated acceptance, not actual screening uptake, diagnostic outcomes, or a clinical treatment effect.'),
176:('Which accelerometer activity-classification methods are reproducible at population scale?','A scoping review screened 1,851 records and included 158 validated activity-classification studies.','Machine and deep learning predominated, but laboratory validation dominated; only 16 studies supplied public code and two examined seasonality.','The review maps reporting and validation gaps rather than providing a pooled accuracy estimate or selecting a universally superior classifier.'),
177:('Do deployed cardiovascular AI interventions improve workflow and patient outcomes?','A systematic review identified 32 randomized trials, with 27 meta-analyzed across workflow, engagement, and clinical-outcome tiers.','Pooled estimates favored shorter workflows, better adherence, and lower all-cause mortality for decision-support implementations.','Interventions and endpoints vary; restricted blinding and scarce sham-AI controls limit attribution and generalization of pooled benefits.'),
178:('Can AI standardize parenteral nutrition after hematopoietic transplantation?','A supervised dosing model and reinforcement-learning policy use daily clinical states and a library of 30 nutrition regimens.','Records from 1,473 TPN-treated adults covering 27,447 patient-days supported next-day dosing correlation near 0.71 and higher retrospective composite policy scores.','Off-policy scores do not demonstrate safer nutrition or improved patient outcomes; prospective evaluation remains necessary.'),
179:('Does deep-learning assistance improve routine cervical cytology reading?','Four less-experienced cytopathologists interpreted slides from 1,920 women in a multicenter randomized crossover reader study.','Assistance improved sensitivity from 71.3% to 85.7%, preserved specificity, and substantially shortened reading time.','Randomization concerned slide-reading sequences, not allocation of women to clinical care; downstream screening outcomes were not established.'),
})
add({
180:('Can dental radiographs support objective assessment of implant esthetic-risk markers?','A multifunctional deep-learning system detects inflammation, adjacent restorations, and contact-point-to-bone distance, with reader, collaboration, prospective, and multisite evaluations.','AI improved distance assessment and task-specific dentist collaboration, with consistent specificity across settings.','The measured targets are radiographic surrogates; actual postoperative esthetic outcomes were not prospectively measured.'),
181:('How well do MRI models and physicians predict glioma IDH status across populations?','ResNet34 and vision-transformer models were compared with 18 physicians on benchmark and Japanese external data.','The transformer achieved benchmark AUC 0.97 but external AUC 0.82 with poor calibration; high-performing physicians reached 0.88 with better calibration.','Strong benchmark discrimination concealed external degradation; model superiority cannot be assumed in a new clinical domain.'),
182:('Do radiology AI devices receive coherent lifecycle safety management after approval?','A regulatory-record analysis linked 956 FDA-approved devices with software updates, adverse events, and recalls.','About 44.9% had updates, while software-related safety events and corrective updates showed incomplete linkage, motivating closed-loop lifecycle oversight.','Public regulatory records reflect reported events and documentation; missing linkage is not a direct estimate of every device’s safety or manufacturer practice.'),
183:('Can ultrasound characterize breast cancer molecular subtypes before biopsy?','MUST-Sub fuses B-mode morphology with contrast-enhanced ultrasound dynamics through a spatiotemporal transformer.','Internal, prospective, and multicenter external cohorts showed macro-AUCs of 0.94, 0.90, and 0.92; attention-derived biomarkers correlated with tumor size and proliferation.','Subtype prediction is an adjunct, not evidence that imaging can safely replace tissue-based molecular testing or improve treatment outcomes.'),
184:('Can incomplete or complete multiphase CT distinguish difficult renal tumor classes?','MPANet integrates clinical information with attention across available contrast-enhanced CT phases.','Among 1,688 multicenter cases, internal macro-AUC was 0.850 and external values were 0.811 and 0.813, with higher accuracy than compared radiologist assessments.','Reader comparisons and retrospective classification do not establish treatment benefit; grouping oncocytic tumors also limits finer subtype resolution.'),
185:('Does gastrointestinal specialization improve pathology foundation-model utility?','Digepath combines pretraining on 210,043 slides and over 353 million patches with expert-region fine-tuning and an agent reasoning framework.','It led 32 of 33 gastrointestinal downstream tasks spanning diagnosis, molecular profiling, and prognosis.','Broad benchmark success and a proposed diagnostic agent do not establish prospective workflow safety or improved clinical outcomes.'),
186:('Can hospitals extract cancer phenotypes from long pathology reports without cloud processing?','OncoPT adapts Longformer and BigBird to 4,096-token oncology reports and five registry phenotypes.','Breast and gastric cancer evaluations showed strong private-dataset F1 and gains over commercial chatbots on CORAL, supporting onsite information extraction.','Local deployment potential is not a comprehensive privacy guarantee; extraction quality and transfer require site-specific validation.'),
187:('Do hospital AI governance frameworks specify practical oversight across the lifecycle?','A PRISMA-ScR review compared 77 acute-care frameworks across principles, assessment, lifecycle coverage, and oversight.','Only ten contained all four components, while explicit oversight mechanisms appeared in 15, revealing a gap between principles and operational governance.','Framework completeness is not evidence of effectiveness; implementation and real-world impact still need evaluation.'),
188:('How much medical AI evidence has advanced beyond preclinical development?','A scoping synthesis extracted 4,667 primary studies from 218 recent systematic reviews and classified stage, geography, specialty, and design.','Only 2.4% were randomized trials; most were single-center and many lacked reported guideline adherence, alongside concentrated geography and frequent favorable outcomes.','These are review-derived studies from a defined sampling window, not a census of all medical AI publications or this website’s corpus.'),
189:('Can lightweight language models improve report classification without losing reasoning quality?','Disease-label supervised fine-tuning is followed by group-relative policy optimization targeting accuracy and output format.','Across three radiologist-annotated datasets, reinforcement learning improved classification beyond supervised tuning and increased reasoning recall and comprehensiveness.','The abstract supplies no numeric effect sizes or clinical deployment evaluation; report-label performance is not patient diagnostic benefit.'),
})
add({
190:('Can automated CT volumetry quantify atelectasis after right upper lobectomy?','Three nnU-Net segmentation models measure postoperative lobar and airway changes against radiological grades.','In 236 retrospectively studied patients, middle-lobe volume loss tracked atelectasis severity, while normalized volume changes were associated with subsequent bronchoscopy requirements.','Single-cohort associations do not establish that automated measurements improve postoperative management or replace clinical assessment.'),
191:('Can medical vision-language reasoning be learned with much less annotation?','ConceptVLM uses a structured medical concept dictionary and masked attention to focus general-model fine-tuning.','Medical multimodal benchmarks showed leading performance using 1% of the original training data while preserving reasoning and response diversity.','Benchmark data efficiency does not establish diagnostic reliability, calibration, or safety in clinical workflows.'),
192:('Can reinforcement learning safely automate ciprofol delivery for endoscopy?','An automated anesthesia controller was developed on 509 participants and evaluated against clinician management in a four-center randomized trial with 418 participants.','Hypoxemia rates were similar, induction was faster, and drug use and recovery were comparable; intraoperative movement increased.','Results apply to the studied lower-risk adults and procedure setting; the abstract’s trial registration date follows the reported recruitment start.'),
193:('How accurately do digital clock-drawing tests identify cognitive impairment?','A diagnostic meta-analysis synthesized 13 studies covering 17 tests, including algorithmic and traditional scoring.','Pooled standalone performance was lower for mild cognitive impairment than Alzheimer disease, with summary AUCs 0.825 and 0.928, respectively.','Notable study bias, variable test augmentation, and exploratory subgroup comparisons limit conclusions about algorithm superiority or routine screening impact.'),
194:('Does a Korean ECG AI generalize to a large US health system?','External validation evaluated ten emergency and cardiac biomarkers using Mayo Clinic Platform records and prespecified AUC benchmarks.','AUCs ranged from 0.883 to 0.949; a paired 1,368-person subset outperformed initial troponin for myocardial-infarction targets.','Retrospective external discrimination does not establish prospective triage benefit; calibration and clinical integration still require evaluation.'),
195:('Can delivery mode after labor induction be predicted across health systems?','Models were developed on 2,434 Portuguese records, with a simplified 13-feature logistic model tested on 10,591 Consortium on Safe Labor records.','External AUROC reached 0.808, but calibration underestimated cesarean risk by 10–75% despite favorable decision-curve results.','Outcome imbalance and miscalibration constrain counseling utility; external discrimination alone does not justify clinical adoption.'),
196:('Can a new neural architecture improve extraction of biomedical entities?','FRKAN-BioNER combines BioBERT representations with a Fourier Kolmogorov-Arnold network.','Nine public datasets yielded F1 scores ranging from 78.58% to 93.12%, exceeding several compared approaches for disease, drug, and gene recognition.','Entity-recognition benchmarks support text mining, not validated clinical decision-making or demonstrated improvements in knowledge-graph use.'),
197:('Can TikTok discussions improve population opioid-mortality forecasting?','LDA topics from 569,581 comments on 48,306 videos augment ARIMA forecasts, with dictionary and language-model analysis of discourse.','Adding discussion topics reduced six-month forecasting error by up to 37% and revealed use, recovery, harm-reduction, and bereavement themes.','Platform-selected conversation is not representative patient surveillance; retrospective forecasting associations require prospective robustness checks.'),
198:('How mature is passive digital sensing for dementia screening?','A systematic review synthesized 30 studies using real-world passive sensor data for Alzheimer disease and related dementias.','Wearable motion and pulse sensing predominated, with promising reported performance but mostly internal validation, heterogeneous reference standards, and very limited public data sharing.','Cross-study accuracy summaries do not establish externally validated population screening; small and uneven cohorts constrain generalization.'),
199:('Can digital behavior help identify peripartum depressive symptoms?','A systematic review examined 14 studies of passive sensing, language, mood logs, and ecological momentary assessments.','Sleep and circadian measures were frequently associated with symptoms; activity findings varied, while active data often added information alongside history and self-report.','Observational, heterogeneous, exploratory evidence prevents causal interpretation and requires stronger external validation before clinical prediction.'),
})
add({
200:('Can retinal disease classifiers use angiographic knowledge without dye imaging at deployment?','Paired color photographs and fluorescein angiograms train disentangled representations and disease-specific reference libraries.','Across 119,173 images and seven diseases, internal and external AUCs reached 0.98 and 0.96 using photographs alone at inference.','High classification accuracy does not establish equivalence to angiography for every vascular assessment or justify replacing indicated diagnostic procedures.'),
201:('Do hospital-specific models outperform multicenter learning for postoperative kidney injury?','Local models were compared with pooled training and federated model stacking across a national research network.','Among 43,926 cardiac-surgery cases from 23 hospitals, multicenter approaches improved temporal and external prediction across kidney-injury severities, particularly at smaller hospitals.','Prediction gains do not demonstrate improved prevention, and federated implementation still requires local calibration and privacy assessment.'),
202:('Can observational trial emulation strengthen evidence for AI embryo selection?','The FEMI embryo model was evaluated using propensity matching and S-learner treatment-effect estimation in 4,674 multicenter cases.','FEMI risk scores remained associated with implantation failure after measured-confounder adjustment, including maternal age, and generalized externally.','Target-trial emulation relies on unmeasured-confounding assumptions; estimated effects are not results of an actual randomized embryo-selection intervention.'),
203:('How reliable are prediction models for lupus manifestations and mortality?','A systematic review and meta-analysis assessed 89 models from 35 studies using PROBAST.','Performance varied by outcome and often declined at validation; all models had high risk of bias and most showed low applicability, despite some high reported AUCs.','Geographic concentration and methodological weaknesses limit clinical transfer; the abstract also contains an internally inconsistent development AUC interval.'),
204:('Can language models reason causally about contextualized laboratory results?','GPT-o1 and Llama-3.2-8b answered 99 scenarios covering association, intervention, and counterfactual reasoning, rated by four medically trained experts.','GPT-o1 had higher overall AUROC and reasoning scores, while both models struggled with altered-outcome counterfactuals.','Expert-rated simulated cases do not establish reliable causal inference or safety in real patient laboratory interpretation.'),
205:('Can MRI models separate mild-cognitive-impairment signatures from normal aging?','A conditional variational autoencoder learns disease-specific latent structural features across BABRI and ADNI cohorts.','Analyses of 918 and 1,293 participants supported cognitive associations and Alzheimer-conversion prediction at AUC 0.83, exceeding compared atrophy and CSF measures.','Latent disentanglement and prediction do not prove removal of every confounder or establish a disease-specific causal mechanism.'),
206:('Can personalized wearable physiology track post-vaccination inflammation?','An individualized multivariate change index from torso patches was compared with serum biomarkers and symptoms.','Sixty-one volunteers receiving 80 vaccine doses showed moderate correlations with CRP, interferon-gamma, and reactogenicity across the monitoring period.','Correlation in a small vaccination cohort does not establish interchangeability with blood tests or validity across inflammatory diseases.'),
207:('How does hospitalization disrupt sleep and circadian physiology after cardiac surgery?','Eleven remote sensors collected environmental and physiological data before, during, and after admission.','Thirteen patients generated 1.8 million observations; nighttime disturbance, wakefulness, and transient cognitive impairment accompanied altered rhythms.','The small observational feasibility sample cannot establish causal effects; sensor observations are not independent patients or evidence of an effective AI intervention.'),
208:('Can confocal endomicroscopy accelerate intraoperative brain-tumor diagnosis, with AI support?','A multicenter prospective study compared confocal imaging with frozen sections and developed a Swin-transformer diagnostic model.','Among 461 biopsies from 376 patients, confocal accuracy was comparable with faster turnaround; AI achieved 0.94 tumor-detection and 0.88 subtype accuracy.','Prospective imaging collection does not by itself prove a frozen AI model was prospectively validated or that AI improved surgical outcomes.'),
209:('Can a neurology-specific language model support emergency diagnosis?','Xuanwu-NeuroAid underwent prospective shadow evaluation in 433 patients, with diagnosis comparison and blinded recommendation ratings.','Model accuracy was 79.4% versus physicians’ 65.4%, and experts rated its recommendations more favorably; demographic inputs altered education advice.','Shadow and simulated decision comparisons do not demonstrate benefits from clinicians acting on model outputs or resolve demographic sensitivity.'),
})
add({
210:('Can slide-level AI distinguish early pregnancy-loss subtypes, including molar pregnancy?','An adaptive-masking patch-to-slide fusion model combines histology and immunohistochemical stains.','Multicenter data from 1,287 patients yielded independent-test accuracy 0.801 and AUROC 0.930; combined H&E/p57 models and AI assistance improved diagnostic performance.','Slide counts differ from patient counts; improved classification does not establish reduced testing costs or better pregnancy-related outcomes.'),
211:('Are AI-generated medical teaching images clinically faithful and demographically balanced?','A PRISMA-guided review synthesized 36 empirical evaluations, predominantly of DALL-E tools.','Three quarters reported demographic skew, while 17 identified clinical-fidelity problems such as anatomical errors and incorrect equipment, sometimes concealed by visual plausibility.','The review assesses generated-image risks, not a randomized educational intervention or measured learner harm.'),
212:('Can real-time AI improve completeness of upper-airway endoscopy?','ENDOVISTA-ENT tracks anatomical coverage, trained on videos from 3,630 patients and tested in a two-center patient-randomized trial.','Among 318 participants, assisted examinations covered 93.08% versus 83.50% of predefined sites without significantly longer procedures.','The system monitors examination quality rather than lesions; better coverage does not directly establish fewer missed cancers or improved patient outcomes.'),
213:('Can ultrasound AI reduce operator variation in detecting focal liver lesions?','Auto-DFLLs combines ResNet and feature-pyramid detection using 5,258 prospectively collected videos from three hospitals.','Internal AP50 was 0.7772; assisted reader evaluations improved junior and senior sonographer detection, including small lesions.','Prospective video acquisition is distinct from prospective validation of a locked model; reader gains do not establish real-world screening benefit.'),
214:('How strongly does prompting alter language-model hypertension recommendations and physician decisions?','Multiple prompting strategies were tested on 300 simulated cases, followed by physician-assistance comparisons.','Best prompting reached 91.3% model accuracy and improved physician decisions, while poor configurations increased inappropriate regimens and reduced baseline performance.','Simulated case decisions are not treatment outcomes; the results show configuration-dependent risk rather than uniformly beneficial LLM assistance.'),
215:('Can agents automate evidence-grounded pharmacogenomic recommendations?','A modular LLM pipeline retrieves literature and FDA labels, extracts entities, aggregates evidence, and generates phenotype-specific gene-drug guidance.','Entity extraction reached 91.9% across 22 articles; experts favored the system over leading LLM baselines on 24 sampled recommendations.','Small expert-rated samples do not establish comprehensive guideline coverage, safe prescribing, or improved outcomes across gene-drug contexts.'),
216:('Can clinical-note context improve reinforcement-learning sepsis policies?','MORE-CLEAR uses LLM note embeddings with gated multimodal fusion and cross-modal attention for offline policy learning.','Cross-validation on MIMIC-III, MIMIC-IV, and SNUH data improved estimated survival and policy scores relative to structured-only approaches.','Estimated off-policy survival is not observed benefit from administering recommended treatments; confounding and evaluation assumptions remain central.'),
217:('How do anonymization and synthetic claims affect medication-safety analyses?','A case study compares privacy, fidelity, and hazard-ratio reproducibility under different attack and sharing assumptions.','Both transformed datasets broadly reproduced original findings but increased uncertainty, with greater utility linked to greater privacy risk.','Results depend on one small high-dimensional dataset and threat models; synthetic data should not be assumed inherently anonymous or analytically equivalent.'),
218:('Can wearable ECG and pulse sensing translate anxiety detection into routine care?','A systematic review compares 38 studies of sensing protocols, induction paradigms, and statistical or learned analytics.','Autonomic markers consistently reflected anxiety-related changes, but heterogeneous, laboratory-centered studies rarely established real-world utility or patient impact.','Physiological association and laboratory classification do not establish disorder-specific diagnosis or effective continuous clinical monitoring.'),
219:('Can facial expressions provide a nonverbal estimate of headache intensity?','Face detection and landmark networks extract action units, with peak-expression frames combined into a headache pain index.','In 80 adults at one institution, the index correlated moderately with self-reported moderate-to-severe pain, with correlations around 0.41–0.52.','Cross-sectional associations and peak-frame selection limit generalization; facial estimates cannot replace patient-reported pain or establish longitudinal monitoring validity.'),
})
add({
220:('Can pathology AI identify the origin of metastatic malignancy across specimen types?','Soft multiclass feature augmentation learns data-efficient slide representations from histology, cytological smears, and cell blocks.','Evaluations on 1,196 histology, 260 smear, and 129 cell-block slides outperformed four compared methods for common metastatic origins.','These are slide-level benchmarks; the abstract does not establish diagnostic utility specifically in unresolved cancer-of-unknown-primary patients or better treatment outcomes.'),
221:('Can one imaging model support multiple acute-stroke triage tasks?','A unified encoder-decoder combines noncontrast CT, angiography, and perfusion with symmetry, vascular graphs, and temporal fusion.','Multicenter testing improved vessel-occlusion detection, collateral scoring, and infarct segmentation; reported PACS deployment achieved sub-minute inference and fewer triage errors.','The abstract does not specify an intervention-controlled design for claimed transfer and triage effects or provide patient counts.'),
222:('Can noninvasive wearable signals personalize cardiovascular digital twins?','Windkessel physics-informed neural networks embed cardiovascular differential equations into bioimpedance-based blood-pressure modeling.','Healthy and hypertensive datasets showed 12–25% lower prediction error than data-driven networks; synthetic waveforms supported accurate compliance and resistance estimation.','Synthetic parameter recovery is distinct from measuring true physiological parameters in patients; clinical monitoring utility requires further validation.'),
223:('Can a shared multimodal representation unify lung-nodule diagnosis and prognosis?','VITALIS combines image-text graphs, guided attention, and neural differential equations with task-specific detection, classification, count, and survival heads.','Three public cohorts supported localization, malignancy assessment, calibrated survival estimates, and consistent counts across tasks.','The abstract lacks numeric effect sizes and patient counts; benchmark coherence does not establish clinical decision benefit.'),
224:('Where could machine learning improve osteoporosis screening?','A narrative review discusses opportunistic screening, individualized risk assessment, and quantitative bone-quality analysis.','It outlines promising applications and implementation barriers relevant to earlier detection and fracture-risk assessment.','This is a strategic narrative synthesis, not a systematic evidence appraisal, pooled diagnostic estimate, or proof of reduced fractures.'),
225:('Can a bilingual-language digital twin select the best language for aphasia therapy?','A double-blind randomized trial assigned 48 Spanish-English speakers to 40 hours of treatment in the BiLex-recommended or opposite language.','Treated-language gains were similar, while opposite-language assignment produced greater but more variable cross-language generalization; subgroup differences aligned with model predictions.','The primary comparison does not support uniform superiority of the recommended language; subgroup results require cautious interpretation.'),
226:('How well does elderly-ICU mortality prediction transfer internationally, and can updating help?','ELDER-ICU underwent external validation across 12 centers with recalibration, incremental learning, and retraining comparisons.','Discrimination remained stronger in US and Austrian cohorts than Asian sites; retraining improved Asian AUROCs and calibration methods helped globally.','Updating performance on existing data does not establish improved critical-care decisions or prospective robustness after future shifts.'),
227:('Can agents suggest lower-cost prescriptions while retaining therapeutic suitability?','EcoRxAgent retrieves substitutes, constructs candidate regimens, checks safety, and compares costs.','Across two cohorts totaling 1,559 prescriptions, assessed substitutes were therapeutically non-inferior to original prescriptions and reduced calculated costs by 14.40–40.14%.','Prescription-level equivalence and calculated savings are not observed patient treatment outcomes, real purchasing savings, or a randomized prescribing trial.'),
228:('Does an AI prognosis tool improve clinician assessment of colorectal liver metastases?','Twelve surgical oncologists evaluated 166 retrospective cases with and without assistance in a randomized crossed reader design.','Across 3,984 assessments, assistance improved three-year mortality AUC by 0.091, shortened decision time, and increased confidence, especially among less-experienced readers.','Prospective reader recruitment does not make underlying cases prospective, and clinician assessment gains do not establish patient survival benefit.'),
229:('Can eye-surface microvascular video support noninvasive blood-count estimates?','Video-to-Vessels compresses conjunctival video into vessel representations; VesselNet uses convolutional features and cross-attention for regression.','Among 224 participants with paired laboratory counts, anemia AUC was 0.828 and hemoglobin/RBC correlations were moderate; stabilization and denoising materially helped.','The results are preliminary and do not validate a complete blood count or establish replacement of venous laboratory testing.'),
})
add({
230:('Can ECG models estimate ejection fraction and screen systolic dysfunction?','Convolutional and probabilistic networks use ECG alone or structured features, with personalized variants.','Among 191,941 patients and 236,623 ECG/echo pairs, personalization lowered mean absolute errors; systolic-dysfunction detection reached AUC 0.88 and sensitivity 0.92.','Repeated pairs are not independent patients; high negative predictive value depends on prevalence and does not establish replacement of echocardiography.'),
231:('Can generative AI produce safe teaching cases about psychiatric chatbot use?','ChatGPT-5 Pro generated psychiatric vignettes rated by three board-certified psychiatrists for relevance, diagnostic information, explanations, and safety.','Relevance and diagnostic sufficiency were rated highly, but safety ratings were weaker, indicating a need for expert review.','This small expert evaluation does not establish educational effectiveness, learner outcomes, or safety of patient-facing chatbot use.'),
232:('Can rapid saliva profiling identify periodontitis co-occurring with diabetes?','PESI mass-spectrometry fingerprints and demographic covariates feed a lightweight liquid neural network.','Among 426 participants split into training and test sets, test accuracy reached 91.9%, with full recall for the comorbid group and fewer parameters than recurrent alternatives.','A random split within a two-center feasibility sample is not independent prospective screening validation; the small subgroup limits certainty.'),
233:('Can simple interpretable models improve stroke-risk prediction after new atrial fibrillation?','Logistic regression and calibrated gradient boosting use age, comorbidities, and medication information, with external validation.','External AUCs of 0.877–0.886 exceeded CHA2DS2-VASc, with favorable calibration and risk stratification.','Observed treatment responsiveness and decision curves do not establish that model-guided anticoagulant initiation improves outcomes or safely changes treatment thresholds.'),
234:('Can a physics-informed digital twin infer cerebral vascular regulation from limited measurements?','CereBRLSIM combines physiological mechanisms with latent-state inference using experimental, simulated, and patient data.','Personalization to six neurocritical-care patients distinguished pressure-flow phenotypes and improved blood-flow forecasting compared with machine-learning baselines.','The tiny clinical sample and partly simulated validation cannot establish reliable outcome prediction or benefit from personalized treatment targets.'),
235:('Can one pretrained model provide reusable representations across 3D MRI tasks?','Decipher-MR combines self-supervised visual learning and report supervision, attaching lightweight task decoders to a frozen encoder.','Training used 200,000 series from over 22,000 studies; evaluated classification, localization, demographic, and retrieval tasks improved over compared models.','MRI series and studies are not patient counts; results apply to the tested datasets rather than universal anatomical or clinical generalization.'),
236:('Can language-model reformulation improve mapping ambiguous biomedical mentions to standard concepts?','A neural-symbolic agent expands abbreviations and clarifies descriptions before terminology linking.','MedMentions, ST21pv, and MCN benchmarks improved Recall@1, including gains up to 24.8 points for zero-shot abbreviations; human raters supported most generated expansions.','Incorrect expansions remain possible, and concept-linking benchmark accuracy does not establish safe downstream clinical coding or decision support.'),
237:('Can a vision-language system jointly assess bone, airway, and occlusion after facial trauma?','HoloTrauma 3X integrates multimodal triadic reasoning for robot-assisted reconstruction across institutional datasets.','The abstract reports evaluation involving 8,427 trauma patients, submillimeter skeletal errors, shorter operations, and fewer intraoperative complications.','The abstract does not specify allocation or comparator adjustment; reported operative reductions should not be interpreted as a proven randomized causal effect.'),
238:('Can a specialized guardrail detect psychiatric crises in text conversations?','VMHG was benchmarked against general guardrails on 1,800 simulated clinician-labeled messages and 794 mental-health messages from NVIDIA Aegis.','Sensitivity remained near 0.99 across datasets, but external specificity fell to 0.859, revealing a false-positive tradeoff.','Message-level classification is not prospective crisis prevention or evidence that downstream chatbot responses are clinically safe.'),
239:('Can clinicians refine liver segmentation by selecting candidates instead of drawing corrections?','UAIR generates uncertainty-informed segmentation alternatives and iteratively aligns outputs with user selections.','A multicenter CT evaluation reported Dice 0.776 versus 0.685 for manual positional prompting, with fewer prompting interactions.','Segmentation agreement and interaction counts do not establish better treatment decisions; clinical preference alignment may vary across users and institutions.'),
})
add({
240:('Can a glioma vision-language model predict molecular status and draft MRI reports?','Glio-LLaMA-Vision combines biomedical image-text pretraining with 1,001 institutional training patients and multiple internal/external cohorts.','IDH prediction AUCs ranged from 0.85 to 0.95; neuroradiologists judged 91% of generated reports clinically acceptable, though report-text metrics declined externally.','Clinical acceptability is not error-free reporting; only 37.8% matched or exceeded original-report quality, and workflow benefit remains untested.'),
241:('Can a single clinical language model handle several structured-record prediction tasks?','A seven-billion-parameter LLaMA-based Hopkins model was fine-tuned using 42,160 patients and externally evaluated across three systems.','Four tasks involving 1,329 external patients yielded mean ROC-AUC 0.84 and improved on zero-shot language-model baselines.','Predictive discrimination across selected tasks does not establish safe treatment recommendations, prospective usefulness, or integration without substantial local validation.'),
242:('Can language models simplify Chinese surgical consent while retaining essential information?','Forms from nine hospitals were compared in original, LLM-simplified, and clinician-revised versions using readability, quality, and lay comprehension assessments.','LLM simplification improved comprehension but weakened risk-information quality; clinician revision restored accuracy and produced the strongest comprehension scores.','Document and comprehension assessments do not establish legally sufficient consent or improved real surgical decision-making without clinician oversight.'),
243:('Can language models make radiology reports easier for patients to understand?','A two-stage study assessed 320 reports and then 800 patients, comparing three models and demographic interactions.','Simplified reports improved comprehension and reduced reported anxiety in the studied setting; education and age influenced benefit.','Missing anatomical details and inconsistent outputs require review; the abstract does not establish randomized causal effects or uniform benefit across demographic groups.'),
244:('Can language models predict complications after vertebral kyphoplasty?','GPT-5 and DeepSeek R1 were compared with conventional models and surgeons using retrospective and prospective single-hospital data.','Performance was more favorable for cement leakage than new fractures; an RBF-SVM led fracture prediction, while LLM explanations helped surgeons only for leakage.','Low correlation-based metrics, poor subtype predictions, and limited-site evaluation caution against interpreting high leakage F1 as broad clinical readiness.'),
245:('Does real-time polyp-detection AI improve adenoma detection in experienced outpatient practices?','A multicenter randomized trial compared EndoMind-assisted and conventional colonoscopy across five centers and ten experienced examiners.','Among 914 intention-to-treat participants, adenoma detection was 34.5% versus 32.9%, without a significant difference.','This null trial does not establish benefit in the studied setting; effects may differ by examiner experience and population, requiring appropriately designed external studies.'),
246:('How should medical language-model benchmarks be selected and designed?','A scoping review of 55 studies produced a structured taxonomy and the READY framework, checked by five domain experts.','The framework emphasizes reliability, ethics, annotation, diversity, and validated usefulness, with consistent expert agreement on application.','Agreement about a framework is not evidence that its adoption improves model safety or predicts real clinical performance.'),
247:('Can breath and saliva biomarkers support noninvasive oral-cancer detection?','AI integrates breath mass spectrometry with salivary metagenomic features, including methanethiol and Fusobacterium signals.','A 222-person discovery cohort and 83-person external cohort supported discrimination of oral squamous-cell carcinoma from healthy controls, with external AUC 0.92.','Case-control discrimination does not establish population-screening predictive value or performance against benign oral disease and other clinically relevant alternatives.'),
248:('Can deep learning harmonize PET measurements across PET-MRI and PET-CT platforms?','An anatomically guided transformer learns CT-anchored attenuation features, contrastive alignment, and residual correction.','Seventy paired same-day cases and 420 multicenter validation cases showed substantially reduced tracer quantification bias, including amyloid Centiloid discrepancy reduction from 23.6 to 4.1.','Reduced measurement discrepancy is not proof of improved diagnoses or treatment outcomes; residual differences and unseen acquisition conditions still matter.'),
249:('Can multimodal AI generate reliable draft upper-gastrointestinal endoscopy reports?','Report-Angel combines a multimodal language model and conventional image models trained on 20,617 image-text pairs.','Prospective internal and external cohorts yielded clinically acceptable reports in 79.3% and 83.3%; case-level accuracy and completeness remained imperfect despite rapid processing.','These are draft reports requiring clinician review; prospective reporting accuracy does not establish patient benefit or elimination of reporting errors.'),
})

